1521017.steps:
1. Policy \ DNS Security \ Settings \ DNS Filtering \ Custom Domain, add a domain: www.ea.com, Category-4. Malware;
2. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add top: a policy named Test, Interface-X0, action-Filter, Profile-Default Profile, Enable;
3. PC connect to X0, set the DNS of PC as X0 IP;
4. From PC, dig www.ea.com, do capture packet on DUT;
5. Check the DNS Packets;
6. Delete the custom domain www.ea.com, repeat 4-5.

1521014.steps:
1. Add some custom domains(over 3 entries), one of them named test.com;
2. Show one custom domain: # show dns-security dns-filtering custom-domain test.com
3. Show all custom domains: # show dns-security dns-filtering custom-domains

1521013.steps:
1. From CLI, enter config mode;
2. Add some custom domains(over 3 entries);
3. Delete all custom domains: # dns-security # dns-filtering # no custom-domains # commit

1521003.steps:
1. Policy \ DNS Security \ Settings \ DNS Filtering \ Custom Domain, add a domain: Domain-*.ea.com, Category-1.Adult;
2. Add a duplicate domain: *.ea.com;
3. Add a invalid domain: !@#.222 .

1521003.result:
In step 1, success;
In step 2, error prompts: Already exists.
In step 3, error prompts: failed : Invalid domain: !@#.222

1521050.steps:
1. Profile Objects \ DNS Filtering, add a profile named "test", the action of category "Gaming" is Forged IP reply;
2. Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules
, enable a DNS Policy : Action-Filter, Interface-X0, Profile-"test"; 3.Policy \ DNS Security \ DNS Filtering, set a valid Forged IP address 10.0.0.1/1001::1; 4. PC connected to X0, set dns server as X0 IP, do 'dig www.ea.com -t CNAME(/TXT/MX/NS)', check the result.

